      "id": 1,
      "text": "Gibson was founded in 1858 as the seat of the newly formed Glascock County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gibson%2C_Georgia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town takes its name from Judge William Gibson, a Confederate colonel who donated $500 for the first courthouse.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gibson%2C_Georgia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Gibson was incorporated as a town in 1913 and later became a city in 1943.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gibson%2C_Georgia"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Glascock County Courthouse in Gibson is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gibson%2C_Georgia"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Rocky Comfort Creek, a southeast‑flowing tributary of the Ogeechee River, passes through Gibson’s northern area.",
